meta {
  name: Transfer - Repeat
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/transfers/{{transferId}}/repeat
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "repeatReason": "Sample clotted"
  }
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); });
}

docs {
  Receiving branch: ask the sender to re-collect (transfer RECEIVED or ACCEPTED -> REPEAT).

  For an INTERNAL transfer the test goes back to the sender in the same transaction:
  - from RECEIVED: the sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT (its
    report never left the sender and stops being hidden);
  - from ACCEPTED: the receiving copy is voided, the report is reset and returns to
    the sender, and the original sample goes to REPEAT. Refused (422
    SAMPLE_RETURN_BLOCKED) when a report at the receiving branch already has a
    validated result (Result Done, Approved, Published), and refused (422
    SAMPLE_SENT_TO_BRANCH) when the receiving branch has itself passed the copy on to
    another branch, partner or outsource centre - it must retrieve it first.
  The transfer update is conditional on its current status: a concurrent change makes
  this fail with 422 INVALID_TRANSFER_TRANSITION instead of overwriting it.
  The sender's referring panel (B2B) is notified once the change has committed.
  The reason is mandatory: `repeatReason` must contain at least one non-space character
  (max 255). Missing, empty, spaces-only or non-text values are refused with 400
  VALIDATION_ERROR and nothing changes. The same applies to the group call.
  Who may act (INTERNAL transfer): only the RECEIVING branch. The caller's active
  branch (the profile they switched to) must be the transfer's destination, otherwise
  403 TRANSFER_WRONG_BRANCH and nothing changes. The same applies to pick-up, receive
  and accept. A caller with no active branch (business admin) is refused too. A group
  action is refused as a whole, never skipped, when any transfer belongs to another
  branch.
  Internal branch transfer rules:
  - Once a sample is SENT_INTERNAL to another branch, the SENDER still sees its
    report in the Technician worklist but it is VIEW-ONLY: every write is refused with
    409 LAB_REPORT_SENT_OUT until the transfer is received or returned.
  - A sent sample accepts ONLY Retrieve from the sender, and only until the
    receiving branch has received it (transfer IN_TRANSIT / PICKED_UP).
  - The receiving branch's Reject / Repeat returns the test to the sender: the
    sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT automatically.

  Group actions with `skipInvalid: true` (bulk Reject / Repeat): a transfer that cannot
  go back is SKIPPED, listed in `skipped` with its reason, and the others still go
  through. Each send-back runs in its own savepoint, so a skipped transfer leaves
  nothing changed. This covers a validated result at the receiver
  (422 SAMPLE_RETURN_BLOCKED) and a copy that was already passed on
  (422 SAMPLE_SENT_TO_BRANCH). Without `skipInvalid` the refusal is raised as an error.
}
